# LF everywhere, on every platform. Windows runners (and Windows
# contributors) default to core.autocrlf=true, whose LF->CRLF checkout
# rewrite breaks this repo in two measured ways (the Windows CI leg of
# Phase-0 Task 8 caught both): the corvid-ffi header drift gate
# byte-diffs the committed corvid.h against the cbindgen render (the
# render is LF), and cbindgen itself reads the checked-out src/*.rs —
# CRLF sources inject \r into every doc comment it embeds in the
# generated header. The golden fixtures' line protocol (smoke.c's
# tokenizer) is equally byte-sensitive. `text=auto` keeps binary
# detection; `eol=lf` pins the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
